  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this exact crash. That crash is a XAML fail-fast (0xc000027b) from ListViewBase::OnKeyDown, raised through nested GettingFocus re-entrancy, and it only happens while a fullscreen game is running. Several archived tickets share the 0xc000027b code or a Windows.UI.Xaml.dll fail-fast, but each has a different trigger. Examples are tab dragging (terminal#15689, terminal#16326), clicking outside the text area (terminal#19667), and a crash in the command palette's ListView (terminal#9648). The other ticket about games, terminal#18040, is a hang tied to a GPU/VRR setting, not a crash. Please file this as a new issue. Attach the dumps from %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CrashDumps; you said you can provide full ones, and they should show the inner exception. Include the DPI-boundary and fullscreen-game details too. As a stopgap, avoid switching focus to Terminal with the keyboard while the game is in exclusive fullscreen. Running the game in borderless windowed mode might also avoid it, but I haven't confirmed that."
